34,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems our budget is tighter than expected, and the way we bill depends heavily on whether the care happens on-site or elsewhere.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The data shows that some previous trials actually reduced readmissions, but other shared efforts struggled with simple logistics like access and completion.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Our staffing is quite uneven; we have significant vacancies in ward nursing, but there is actually some unexpected slack in the midwifery rota.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The physical capacity is a real bottleneck. Our rooms and parking fill up way too fast, and the booking system doesn't even track work that isn't a fixed appointment.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've found that joint ventures can fail if ownership isn't clear, and getting legal agreements with outside surgeries can be a very slow process.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, that slack in midwifery is interesting. If we choose a program, we must ensure it doesn't rely on the ward nurses who are already stretched thin.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, I agree. If we want a program that actually lasts, we should prioritize something with proven patient benefits that doesn't collapse under logistical failures.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I agree. We need a balance where the workload is manageable for the staff available, otherwise the program will fail regardless of the patient benefit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shizue, if the booking system only tracks fixed slots, does that mean those slow legal agreements you mentioned are the only way to make outside coordination official?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, it seems so. Without those formal agreements, coordination with outside surgeries remains informal and likely invisible to our official records, which makes it very fragile.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Given the budget constraints and the billing issues I found, we should be wary of any program that requires significant new floor space or relies on off-site visits.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, that's a fair point, but we shouldn't ignore the readmission data. If a program significantly improves patient outcomes, we must find a way to make it work.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, if we avoid off-site visits and new floor space, we might be limited. However, we must prioritize the midwifery slack if we want to avoid burning out the ward staff.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, if we use the midwifery slack, we might avoid the parking and room bottlenecks too, provided the program doesn't just add more people to the waiting room.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, that is a very thoughtful point. We must be careful not to create a new problem while trying to solve another, especially regarding our physical limits.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I think we are reaching a consensus that we need a program that is financially sustainable, utilizes existing staff slack, and avoids adding pressure to our physical infrastructure.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Exactly. We need a solution that is logically sound and evidence-based, rather than just another well-intentioned project that disappears because it wasn't tracked or sustainable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. We should look for a candidate that aligns with our current staffing capacity and doesn't place an undue burden on the teams already struggling with vacancies.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm on board with that. Let's hope the candidates we see next fit all these criteria so we don't end up with a program that just jams up the system.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree with everyone. Let us move forward with a spirit of cooperation and hope that we can find a program that truly supports both our patients and our hardworking staff.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
