58,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The candidates are a Home Follow-Up Team, a Day Rehabilitation Unit, a Perinatal Support Service, and Chronic Care Coordination. Given the budget and billing, the Perinatal Support Service seems most viable.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Shion,,"I agree with Jonathan. The Home Follow-Up and Chronic Care options risk the logistical and data failures I saw, while the Day Rehab Unit would likely worsen the parking and room bottlenecks Kenji mentioned.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree. The Perinatal Support Service fits perfectly with the slack in the midwifery rota I found, and it avoids adding pressure to the already struggling ward nursing staff.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with you all. The Perinatal Support Service seems like the only one that won't jam up our parking or the booking system, especially if it uses that midwifery slack.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I agree as well. Since it is a joint effort between midwifery and pediatrics, we must ensure the budget and rota are clearly shared so it doesn't fail like previous joint clinics.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that is a vital point. As long as we formalize the budget line and the rota from the start, the Perinatal Support Service is the most fiscally responsible choice.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, your caution is noted. If we establish clear ownership and tracking from day one, we avoid the ""buried initiative"" trap and ensure the program's success is actually measurable.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I feel confident that this choice respects the balance of our workforce. By utilizing the available capacity in midwifery, we can provide a wonderful service without overextending our other teams.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,It really feels like the best fit. It doesn't seem to require the kind of massive space or complex outside data agreements that would cause a total system seizure.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I am glad we have found a path that considers everyone's concerns. Let us proceed with the Perinatal Support Service, keeping a watchful eye on the partnership's stability.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I believe we have a strong consensus. I will cast my vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shion,,I agree. I vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,I also vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I vote for the Perinatal Support Service too!,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I will also cast my vote for the Perinatal Support Service.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
